<title>GERMANY: German Oct/Dec sugar output up at 4.17 mln tonnes.</title>
<headline>German Oct/Dec sugar output up at 4.17 mln tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>German domestic sugar output in the first three months of the 1996/97 (Oct/Sept) season totalled 4.17 million tonnes, rounded, compared with 3.80 million in Oct/Dec 1995, sugar industry association WVZ said on Monday.</p>
<p>The three months are the busiest in the sugar year during the beet campaign, with 95/96 full season output at 3.83 million.</p>
<p>WVZ's montly statistics said December sugar output alone was 782,254 tonnes versus 779,199 a year earlier.</p>
<p>Domestic sugar sales in December amounted to 175,018 tonnes compared with 184,180 in December 1995.</p>
<p>Stocks at the end of December totalled 3.22 million tonnes versus 2.90 previously.</p>
<p>December sugar imports of 4,873 tonnes were down from 15,216 in 1995 while December exports of 143,537 tonnes compared with 121,457 a year earlier.</p>
<p>Cumulative details (in tonnes, whites value) --</p>
<p>				    Oct/Dec 1996	Oct/Dec 1995</p>
<p>    Domestic sugar output     4,169,490	  3,800,651</p>
<p>    Imports			    21,458	     38,865</p>
<p>    Exports			   533,891	    499,606</p>
<p>    Domestic sales		  681,296	    692,770</p>
<p>    Carry-in stocks on Oct 1    239,562	    250,854</p>
<p>-Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
